WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.052 --> 00:00:16.938
Bobbie, and Phyllis were walking slowly inside the tunnel.

2
00:00:17.998 --> 00:00:19.799
They were looking for the boy in the red shirt.

3
00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:23.621
Unlike the other boys, he had not come out of the tunnel.

4
00:00:23.641 --> 00:00:32.036
"If a train comes, stand flat against the wall," said Bobbie.

5
00:00:32.056 --> 00:00:34.257
Her voice sounded odd inside the tunnel walls.

6
00:00:34.277 --> 00:00:36.957
"I want to go back.

7
00:00:38.078 --> 00:00:39.798
I don't like it," said Phyllis.

8
00:00:39.818 --> 00:00:44.799
"I don't care what you say, I won't keep walking in the dark."

9
00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:48.720
"Don't be silly, Phyllis," Peter said.

10
00:00:48.740 --> 00:00:51.881
"I've got half of a candle and some matches."

11
00:00:52.742 --> 00:00:53.802
He listened for a second.

12
00:00:54.862 --> 00:00:55.502
"What's that?"

13
00:00:56.783 --> 00:00:59.083
There was a low, humming noise on the railway line.

14
00:00:59.883 --> 00:01:01.544
The sound grew louder and louder.

15
00:01:02.708 --> 00:01:04.329
"It's a train," said Bobbie.

16
00:01:04.349 --> 00:01:09.973
"Let me go back," cried Phyllis, struggling to get away from Bobbie's hand.

17
00:01:09.993 --> 00:01:12.155
"Don't be scared.

18
00:01:12.875 --> 00:01:14.757
It's quite safe," said Bobbie.

19
00:01:15.758 --> 00:01:16.398
"Stand back."

20
00:01:17.439 --> 00:01:18.119
"Come up here!

21
00:01:18.139 --> 00:01:19.760
There's a space!"

22
00:01:20.161 --> 00:01:20.821
Peter shouted.

23
00:01:21.882 --> 00:01:23.843
The sound of the train was now a roar.

24
00:01:26.465 --> 00:01:30.048
Bobbie dragged Phyllis farther into the tunnel, toward Peter's voice.

25
00:01:31.424 --> 00:01:34.126
There was a small space dug out of the tunnel wall.

26
00:01:34.947 --> 00:01:37.669
They stood there while the train roared louder and louder.

27
00:01:38.670 --> 00:01:40.191
It seemed as if it would deafen them.

28
00:01:42.312 --> 00:01:44.494
In the distance they could see the lights of the train.

29
00:01:45.575 --> 00:01:46.896
They were like a dragon's eyes.

30
00:01:48.177 --> 00:01:49.978
The train was screaming toward them.

31
00:01:50.859 --> 00:01:52.600
Phyllis and Bobbie clung to each other.

32
00:01:54.101 --> 00:01:57.384
The train roared by, light flashing from its windows.

33
00:01:59.008 --> 00:02:01.710
The children felt a blast of hot air and smelled smoke.

34
00:02:02.830 --> 00:02:04.471
Even Peter grabbed Bobbie's arm.

35
00:02:05.792 --> 00:02:09.254
Later he explained that it was "in case she was scared."

36
00:02:10.675 --> 00:02:15.138
Slowly the noise got softer and the lights got smaller and smaller and smaller.

37
00:02:16.199 --> 00:02:18.440
With one last whee!

38
00:02:19.521 --> 00:02:20.641
the train left the tunnel.

39
00:02:20.661 --> 00:02:24.744
"Oh!" said the children together, in a whisper.

40
00:02:27.520 --> 00:02:29.461
Peter lit the candle with a shaking hand.

41
00:02:29.481 --> 00:02:33.462
"Come on," he said, his voice shaking too.

42
00:02:33.482 --> 00:02:35.663
"Oh!" said Phyllis.

43
00:02:35.683 --> 00:02:39.925
"What if the boy with the red shirt was in the way of the train?"

44
00:02:39.945 --> 00:02:43.506
"We must keep looking for him," said Peter.

45
00:02:45.327 --> 00:02:47.828
They went on into the deeper darkness of the tunnel.

46
00:02:48.929 --> 00:02:51.690
Peter went first, holding the candle to light the way.

47
00:02:52.930 --> 00:02:55.751
Suddenly Peter stood still and shouted, "Hello!"

48
00:02:56.092 --> 00:02:57.072
Then he hurried ahead.

49
00:02:58.156 --> 00:03:00.197
When the girls reached him, they saw the boy.

50
00:03:03.317 --> 00:03:05.018
Peter had stopped about a meter from him.

51
00:03:06.138 --> 00:03:08.699
Phyllis saw something red and shut her eyes tight.

52
00:03:09.739 --> 00:03:12.780
The boy in the red shirt was on the ground, beside the tracks.

53
00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:16.401
His eyes were closed, and he did not move.

54
00:03:18.662 --> 00:03:20.122
"Is he dead?"

55
00:03:20.562 --> 00:03:22.883
asked Phyllis, still closing her eyes.

56
00:03:22.903 --> 00:03:25.404
"Dead? No!"

57
00:03:25.944 --> 00:03:26.464
said Peter.

58
00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:29.061
"He's fainted, that's all.

59
00:03:29.521 --> 00:03:30.342
What should we do?"

60
00:03:30.362 --> 00:03:32.383
"Can we move him?"

61
00:03:32.803 --> 00:03:33.443
asked Bobbie.

62
00:03:33.463 --> 00:03:38.246
"I don't know, he's a big fellow," replied Peter.

63
00:03:38.266 --> 00:03:41.588
"How about we put some water on his forehead?"

64
00:03:42.588 --> 00:03:46.350
"We don't have any water, but we have some milk from lunch," Bobbie said.

65
00:03:46.370 --> 00:03:48.191
"Let's try that!"

66
00:03:48.211 --> 00:03:56.456
"Yes, and I think people sometimes rub people's hands to help them wake up," said Phyllis.

67
00:03:57.576 --> 00:04:01.562
So Bobbie splashed warm milk onto his forehead while Peter rubbed the boy's hands.

68
00:04:02.684 --> 00:04:05.909
Then together the three children said, "Please wake up!

69
00:04:06.590 --> 00:04:07.691
Please speak!"
